        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="hero-deck">
            One year ago, the Trump administration deployed an influx of federal immigration enforcement agents in the greater Chicago area. In Evanston, enforcement activity reached unprecedented levels. Neighbors were violently taken from the streets and homes. Those who stood up against federal agents faced tear gas and fierce repression.

In the face of the trauma and violence that has come with Operation Midway Blitz, the Evanston and Northwestern communities have responded. This special issue aims to highlight their stories of resilience. From NU’s campus to neighborhoods across Chicago, community members, organizers and students have come together to protect their own.

Here are their stories.

— Emily Dissanayake, Diversity & Inclusion Editor
